	<td bgcolor="#000000" width="100%" valign="top">
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" > <b>Last round of AC tests for me are in</b></font>
	<p><font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" >Same mob - Level 65 A Sentry of Ro, Sol Ro zone in.<br />
<br />
1694 AC (Unbuffed) = 329.4 Average "hit"<br />
1815 AC (Unbuffed) = 311.7 Average "hit"<br />
1917 AC (Unbuffed) = 295.0 Average "hit"<br />
2112 AC (   Buffed ) = 288.6 Average "hit"<br />
<br />
<br />
Just for reference:<br />
1694 AC = 666 hits, 219374 total damage from hits<br />
1815 AC = 813 hits, 253380 total damage from hits<br />
1917 AC = 507 hits, 149544 total damage from hits<br />
2112 AC = 752 hits, 217004 total damage from hits<br />
<br />
Would have liked to have run the 1917 AC test a little longer, but I ran oom due to lack of clarity.<br />
<br />
<a href="http://bellsouthpwp.net/e/h/ehf/ac%20test%20graph.gif" target="_blank">http://bellsouthpwp.net/e/h/ehf/ac%20test%20graph.gif</a><br />
<br />
Also an interesting note. I still dont think its enough data points heh.  It would appear that AC starts tailing off in effectiveness, when a 200AC jump nets you 2% more mitigation.  But if I take my log of 2112 AC and split it into 2 halves, I get 275 average hit for the first half, and 301 average hit for the 2nd half.  That tells me that one of those 2 halfs was likely either unlucky large hits, or lucky small hits.<br />
<br />
If I only used the first half of the log which was a 275 average hit, then the graph makes basically a perfectly straight line. continuing through 2100 AC.<br />
<br />
It could be that AC effectiveness tails off. It could be that AC effectiveness stays the same and my tests are off. The disparity in the 2 halves of my log of 752 data points says alot to me.</font></p>
	
