	<p><font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" >The chance of a spike is just (% of max hit)^(number of consecutive hits).  Usually this number is 4 so the chance goes down like n^4, which is really fast but not quite exponential.  But it's kind of misleading to just calculate the max hit.  Would 4 max hits minus 1 DI kill you?  2 DI?  How about 3 max hits and one max minus 4 DI?  If you just look at consecutive max hits, the only conclusion is that damage spikes are impossible.  I can't even remember the last time I've been hit for max 3 times in a row.  But obviously damage spikes happen, because you don't need 4 consecutive max hits to instant kill a warrior.</font></p>
	
