<tr>
	<td bgcolor="#000000" width="175" valign="top" nowrap>
	<a name="post1525"></a>
	

	<font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" ><b>Solinar</b></font><br>
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >knows that Warriors are superior</font><br>
	<img src="avatar.php?userid=324&dateline=1051645343" border="0" alt=""><p>
&nbsp;<br>
<a href="showthread.php?postid=1525#post1525"><font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >Post #12</font></a><br>
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" >Registered: Apr 2003<br>
	Location: New Orleans<br>
	Posts: 61</font></td>
	
	<td bgcolor="#000000" width="100%" valign="top">
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" > <b></b></font>
	<p><font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" >Way too many factors involved.<br />
<br />
If you ask a specific instance, the probability could be solved Im sure.<br />
<br />
For instance, right now at 2k AC, most PoP mobs hit me for min about 40-45% of the time.  The remaining 55-60% of hits are pretty evenly spread over the remaining 19 Damage Intervals.<br />
<br />
The odds of any single hit on me being for max damage is 60/19 or 3% of all hits are for max damage.  Considering that there is also a 50% hit rate (50% of swings are misses/dodges/ripos/parrys) that means the actual chance per swing of a max hit landing is around 1.5%<br />
<br />
Chance of being 1 rounded is 1.5%^4 or 0.015^4 X chance at the mob making dual weild and double attack checks.<br />
<br />
Lets guess and say most quadding bosses, quad 50% of rounds.  That means the chances of a round of 4 max hits is 0.0000025% or 1 in 39 million rounds.<br />
<br />
Thats good stuff, but unfortunately not the whole picture, because often a quad of DI = 18-20 will kill you just the same as a quad of DI = 20.  Hitting for near max is enough to kill you.  Also there is the chance of getting a riposte at the same time, and also the chance of Flurry, chance of catching 2 rounds of melee between CHs.<br />
<br />
Its all a game of chance, and lowering the size of hits via AC, or lowering the rate of landed hits via evasive, both are very effective at reducing the chance at bad rounds to a level where they will likely never occur.</font></p>
	
